      "limits": [
        "H1 cash flow is exceptionally seasonal. Never double H1 CFO/FCF; use annual-plus-comparable-interim TTM.",
        "Deferred merchant-booking growth is offset partly by receivables and merchant payables. Removing deferred-booking increases alone penalizes one side of the operating cycle; show all three cash-flow lines.",
        "The author no-growth travel-working-capital sensitivity removes the net of deferred merchant bookings, merchant AP and total AR. Total AR is an imperfect proxy because the selected filing does not separately disclose agency/merchant AR cash movements. It is not a company-normalized FCF metric or an exact maintenance cash requirement.",
        "Cash $6.682bn plus short-term investments $0.445bn does not establish excess cash after $15.426bn deferred bookings and supplier payments; grant no excess-cash bonus in a conservative equity valuation.",
        "B2B revenue growth outpaces B2B EBITDA growth because partner commissions and investments rise. Do not apply B2C margins to B2B revenue.",
        "GAAP Q2 EPS includes nontaxable mark-to-market gains and a lower tax rate; do not annualize $7.16 Q2 EPS.",
        "Canadian DST liability reversal of $71m benefited H1 operating income; distinguish from durable cost leverage."
      ]
    }
